# Shared block: the map-selection dialog opened over a game-setup screen (skirmish and LAN use the same window names).
# A 40% scrim, a raised panel 1000 x 640 at left 460, top 220: title, the System/User maps switch as a segmented control,
# the map list with the preview of the highlighted map beside it (start-position markers placed on it by code), Cancel
# and Accept. The including screen moves its own parent window over the dialog first (hit-testing only descends into
# children of a window under the pointer).
hide $WinGadgetBorder
scrim
dialog left top 460 220 1000 640
window text:GUI:SelectAMapLowerCase left top 484 240 500 32 section
rule left top 484 280 952
window $RadioButtonSystemMaps left top 484 300 220 40 radio
window $RadioButtonUserMaps left top 708 300 220 40 radio
window $ListboxMap left top 484 356 620 400 list
window $WinMapPreview left top 1128 356 308 231
window $ButtonBack left top 484 792 180 44 button
window $ButtonOK left top 1236 792 200 44 primary
